# Feedback loop

This project learns from how you correct it. The `capture-feedback` hook
(`.claude/hooks/capture-feedback.cjs`) watches your prompts and appends **durable
guidance** to `log.md` — so standing instructions don't get lost between sessions.

## What gets captured

- Anything you mark explicitly with `#feedback` in a prompt.
- Standing-instruction signals like "from now on…", "always/never…",
  "make sure to…", "stop doing…", "use X instead of Y".

One-off, task-specific messages are ignored — only durable guidance is logged.
Capture is silent and never blocks your prompt.

## Closing the loop

Periodically run `/feedback-review` to cluster recurring feedback and promote it
into `CLAUDE.md` or `.claude/rules/`, where Claude reads it every session. Use
`/feedback-review --apply` to write the promoted rules and archive the log.

## Privacy

The log lives entirely in this repo (`.claude/feedback/`). Nothing is sent
anywhere. Commit it to share standing guidance with your team, or add
`.claude/feedback/` to `.gitignore` to keep it local.
